WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.608
As the Chen dynasty was about to fall, Xu Deyan worried that the chaos of war would separate him from his wife, Princess Lechang.

00:00:07.958 --> 00:00:14.606
He broke a bronze mirror into two halves; husband and wife each took one half and put it away with great care.

00:00:14.956 --> 00:00:19.516
Put together, the two halves of the bronze mirror formed one perfect, complete circle.

00:00:19.866 --> 00:00:26.466
They agreed that one day they would search for each other in Chang'an, and recognize each other by this half of the bronze mirror.

00:00:26.816 --> 00:00:31.160
They promised to meet again on the fifteenth day of the first month, at the market in Chang'an.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:38.302
After the Chen dynasty fell, the two were indeed separated in the chaos of war, each drifting to a different place.

00:00:38.652 --> 00:00:43.476
Xu Deyan asked everywhere he went, but there was never any news of his wife.

00:00:43.826 --> 00:00:50.786
Many years later, by means of the two halves of the bronze mirror, they finally recognized each other again in the crowd.

00:00:51.136 --> 00:00:59.272
The idiom 'the broken mirror made round again' is used to describe the joy of a husband and wife who are reunited after being separated.

